{#
  ══ WITHDRAWING REFERRAL EARNINGS ═══════════════════════════════════════════════

  A partial, because it is the one part of /account that is a FORM about money and it
  has four mutually exclusive states — requested, available, blocked, and "we do not
  have your bank details yet". Inline in the page those four read as one long card
  with most of it conditionally absent, which is how the wrong one came to be shown.

  It is rendered `only`, with everything it needs passed in, so it cannot quietly
  start depending on a page variable that changes meaning.

  ── THE RULES IT ENFORCES VISUALLY ───────────────────────────────────────────────

  `payout_can` answers "can they" AND "why not" together — see
  `ReferralPayout::available()` — so this never draws a button that will refuse. An
  open request REPLACES the form rather than sitting above it: two ways to ask for
  the same money is how somebody asks twice.

  The bank details are saved once and reused, and each payout keeps its own copy, so
  changing them never alters where an earlier transfer went. That is said out loud
  because it is the question somebody editing this form is actually asking.

  ── THE FIELD RULES, AND WHY THEY ARE NOT SPELLED HERE ───────────────────────────

  Every control is `.ag-field` and `.ag-btn` from the shared library, so the 52px
  height and the 16px face (§11 — anything smaller zooms the viewport on iOS the
  moment it is focused) are enforced in one place rather than re-typed per form.
  This file used to carry its own `.me-input` and `.me-btn`, and they had drifted to
  48px and 14px: a form about money that zooms when you touch it.

  The account-number field is `inputmode="numeric"` and NOT `type="number"`: a
  leading zero is significant in a Nigerian account number and a number input drops
  it. Labels are VISIBLE, not placeholders — a rule stated only in a placeholder is
  stated to nobody, because it vanishes the moment somebody types.
#}

{% import "partials/ui.twig" as ui %}

{% if payout_open %}
  <div class="ag-flash ag-flash--ok" role="status">
    <b>₦{{ payout_open.amount_naira|number_format }} requested</b>
    {% if payout_open.requested_at %}on {{ payout_open.requested_at|slice(0,10) }}{% endif %},
    to {{ payout_open.bank_name|default('your saved account') }}{% if payout_open.account_name %} · {{ payout_open.account_name }}{% endif %}.
    We pay by bank transfer and will be in touch once it has gone.
  </div>

{% elseif payout_can %}
  <form method="post" action="/account/payout" data-ag-validate novalidate class="ag-form">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
    <b class="ag-h2">Withdraw ₦{{ payout_amount|number_format }} to your bank</b>
    <p class="ag-hint">Paid by bank transfer, usually within a few working days. The
      account name has to match your own — a mismatch is the usual reason one is refused.</p>

    <label class="ag-label" for="poBank">Bank</label>
    <input id="poBank" class="ag-field" type="text" name="bank" required maxlength="120"
           autocomplete="off" enterkeyhint="next" placeholder="e.g. GTBank"
           value="{{ payout_bank.bank|default('') }}">

    <label class="ag-label" for="poName">Account name</label>
    <input id="poName" class="ag-field" type="text" name="account_name" required maxlength="160"
           autocomplete="name" enterkeyhint="next"
           value="{{ payout_bank.account_name|default('') }}">

    <label class="ag-label" for="poNum">Account number</label>
    <input id="poNum" class="ag-field ag-field--mono" type="text" name="account_number" required
           inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" maxlength="20" autocomplete="off"
           enterkeyhint="send" value="{{ payout_bank.account_number|default('') }}">

    <button type="submit" class="ag-btn ag-btn--primary">Request payout</button>
  </form>

{% elseif payout_why %}
  <p class="ag-hint">{{ payout_why }}</p>
{% endif %}

{#
  Open by default when there is nothing saved, because then it is not a detail — it
  is the step between a member and their money, and a collapsed `<summary>` reading
  "Save your bank details" is one more thing to discover.
#}
<details class="ag-card ag-disc"{% if not payout_bank.account_number|default('') %} open{% endif %}>
  <summary>{{ payout_bank.account_number|default('') ? 'Change your bank details' : 'Save your bank details' }}</summary>
  <div class="ag-disc__b">
    <p class="ag-hint">
      Saved once and reused for every withdrawal. Each payout keeps its own copy, so
      changing these never alters where an earlier transfer went. We pay by ordinary
      bank transfer — nothing is set up on your behalf with the payment provider.
    </p>
    <form method="post" action="/account/bank" data-ag-validate novalidate class="ag-form">
      <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">

      <label class="ag-label" for="bkBank">Bank</label>
      <input id="bkBank" class="ag-field" type="text" name="bank" required maxlength="120"
             autocomplete="off" enterkeyhint="next" placeholder="e.g. GTBank"
             value="{{ payout_bank.bank|default('') }}">

      <label class="ag-label" for="bkName">Account name</label>
      <input id="bkName" class="ag-field" type="text" name="account_name" required maxlength="160"
             autocomplete="name" enterkeyhint="next"
             value="{{ payout_bank.account_name|default('') }}">
      <p class="ag-hint">It has to be your own name.</p>

      <label class="ag-label" for="bkNum">Account number</label>
      <input id="bkNum" class="ag-field ag-field--mono" type="text" name="account_number" required
             inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" maxlength="20" autocomplete="off"
             enterkeyhint="send" value="{{ payout_bank.account_number|default('') }}">

      <button type="submit" class="ag-btn ag-btn--secondary">Save details</button>
    </form>
  </div>
</details>

{% if payout_history|default([])|length %}
<section class="ag-group">
  <h2>Withdrawals</h2>
  <div class="ag-list">
    {% for h in payout_history %}
      {{ ui.row({
        label: '₦' ~ h.amount_naira|number_format,
        sub: (h.requested_at ? h.requested_at|slice(0,10) : '')
             ~ (h.payment_ref ? ' · ' ~ h.payment_ref : '')
             ~ (h.note ? ' · ' ~ h.note : ''),
        pill: {label: h.status|capitalize,
               tone: h.status == 'paid' ? 'ok' : (h.status == 'rejected' ? 'bad' : 'wait')},
        find: 'payout withdrawal ' ~ h.status
      }) }}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}
